    "/v1/objective-templates": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "List authorized template versions",
        "description": "PROPOSED, not an implemented handler. Authenticate and derive tenant, environment and actor on server. Recheck workload scope and role, template constraints, expected revision and authorization at commit. Require Idempotency-Key for mutations; atomically retain immutable revision/decision/activation, audit and outbox. Changed-key content conflicts. Reject self-approval and stale or future activation. Current objective digest must match the evaluation and recovery decision; never overwrite historical evidence. Paginated reads recheck current disclosure policy. First template creation uses template_id=null and expected_revision=0; a later version identifies that template and the previous revision. Publishing a template makes its versioned bounds available for proposals; it does not approve a workload target. Workload path id and body workload_id must match and resolve within the authenticated scope. Mutation responses are command receipts; a current evaluation and activation remain separate. Responses follow implementation_review/response.schema.json or the named existing domain schema. Authentication, field disclosure, serializers and running handlers still require implementation and acceptance.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "cursor",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "maxLength": 500,
              "pattern": "\\S"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "page_size",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 200
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
